#### Phase 2: Cache Middleware Development (Weeks 3-4)

**Week 3: Core Middleware Implementation**

**Task 3.1: Implement Tenant-Aware Cache Key Generator**

Create `TenantAwareCacheKeyGenerator` that automatically injects tenant prefix into all cache keys:

```java
// Java implementation using Spring Cache
@Component
public class TenantAwareCacheKeyGenerator implements CacheKeyGenerator {

    @Autowired
    private TenantContext tenantContext;

    @Override
    public Object generate(Object target, Method method, Object... params) {
        String tenantId = tenantContext.getCurrentTenantId();
        if (tenantId == null) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Tenant context not available for cache operation");
        }

        // Build cache key with tenant prefix
        StringBuilder keyBuilder = new StringBuilder();
        keyBuilder.append(tenantId).append(":");
        keyBuilder.append(method.getDeclaringClass().getSimpleName()).append(":");
        keyBuilder.append(method.getName());

        for (Object param : params) {
            keyBuilder.append(":").append(param.toString());
        }

        return keyBuilder.toString();
    }
}

// Usage in service layer
@Service
public class BeneficiaryService {

    @Cacheable(value = "beneficiaries", keyGenerator = "tenantAwareCacheKeyGenerator")
    public Beneficiary getBeneficiary(Long beneficiaryId) {
        // Developer writes: beneficiary:123456
        // Middleware generates: TX:BeneficiaryService:getBeneficiary:123456
        return beneficiaryRepository.findById(beneficiaryId);
    }
}
